===== sverb --help
A terminal-native SSH client and server manager with an encrypted vault and optional self-hosted,
end-to-end-encrypted sync

Usage: sverb [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  connect   Launch the TUI with a session open (fuzzy host match or user@host:port)
  join      Join a shared terminal
  hosts     List, add and remove hosts
  keys      Manage SSH keys, or print the effective keymap with --dump
  forward   Run a port-forward rule headless
  snippet   Run snippets on hosts
  import    Import hosts, keys and settings
  export    Export hosts, backups and recordings
  approve   Review and approve locally-acting fields from sync
  agent     Run the built-in agent exposing forwardable vault keys
  lock      Lock the vault
  unlock    Unlock the vault
  login     Log in to a sync server
  logout    Log out of the sync server
  register  Create an account on a sync server
  sync      Sync now or show the sync status
  devices   List or revoke devices
  team      Manage the team vault
  config    Check, print or locate config.toml
  doctor    Diagnose terminal capabilities, agent and sync; list SSH algorithms
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --debug
          Log at debug level and keep recent log lines for the log pane (log files may then contain
          hostnames)

      --workspace <NAME>
          Launch the TUI and open this workspace

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Exit codes:
  0  success
  1  failure
  2  usage error
  3  vault locked or unlock failed
  4  not found (or ambiguous host)
  5  approval required (run `sverb approve <host>`)
  6  network or server error
  7  partial failure

