===== sverb hosts --help
List, add and remove hosts

Usage: sverb hosts [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list  List hosts
  add   Add a host
  rm    Remove a host
  help  Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --debug
          Log at debug level and keep recent log lines for the log pane (log files may then contain
          hostnames)

  -h, --help
          Print help

===== sverb hosts list --help
List hosts

Usage: sverb hosts list [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --debug
          Log at debug level and keep recent log lines for the log pane (log files may then contain
          hostnames)

      --json
          Print JSON (`{"version":1,"data":…}`)

      --tag <TAG>
          Only hosts with this tag (repeatable; all must match)

      --group <GROUP>
          Only hosts in this group

  -h, --help
          Print help

===== sverb hosts add --help
Add a host

Usage: sverb hosts add [OPTIONS] <ADDRESS>

Arguments:
  <ADDRESS>
          Hostname or IP address

Options:
      --debug
          Log at debug level and keep recent log lines for the log pane (log files may then contain
          hostnames)

      --label <LABEL>
          Display label (defaults to the address)

      --user <USER>
          Login user

      --port <PORT>
          SSH port

      --group <GROUP>
          Group to put the host in (must exist unless --create-group)

      --create-group
          Create the group if it does not exist

      --tag <TAG>
          Tag (repeatable; missing tags are created)

  -h, --help
          Print help

===== sverb hosts rm --help
Remove a host

Usage: sverb hosts rm [OPTIONS] <HOST>

Arguments:
  <HOST>
          Label, address or unique fuzzy match

Options:
      --debug
          Log at debug level and keep recent log lines for the log pane (log files may then contain
          hostnames)

  -y, --yes
          Do not ask for confirmation (required without a terminal)

  -h, --help
          Print help

===== sverb keys --help
Manage SSH keys, or print the effective keymap with --dump

Usage: sverb keys [OPTIONS]
       sverb keys <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list      List keys in the vault (no private material)
  generate  Generate a key
  import    Import a key file (OpenSSH, PEM, PKCS#8, or a .pub agent / hardware key)
  export    Export a key
  help      Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --debug
          Log at debug level and keep recent log lines for the log pane (log files may then contain
          hostnames)

      --dump
          Print the effective keymap (built-ins and config overrides)

      --json
          With --dump: print JSON (`{"version":1,"data":…}`)

  -h, --help
          Print help

===== sverb keys list --help
List keys in the vault (no private material)

Usage: sverb keys list [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --debug
          Log at debug level and keep recent log lines for the log pane (log files may then contain
          hostnames)

      --json
          Print JSON (`{"version":1,"data":…}`)

  -h, --help
          Print help

===== sverb keys generate --help
Generate a key

Usage: sverb keys generate [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --debug
          Log at debug level and keep recent log lines for the log pane (log files may then contain
          hostnames)

      --type <KEY_TYPE>
          Key algorithm
          
          [default: ed25519]
          [possible values: ed25519, ecdsa-p256, ecdsa-p384, ecdsa-p521, rsa-2048, rsa-3072,
          rsa-4096]

      --label <LABEL>
          Label for the key

      --comment <COMMENT>
          Key comment (default `user@hostname-sverb`)

      --no-passphrase
          Do not ask for a passphrase (scripts)

  -h, --help
          Print help

